# PCA on Forms of Capital, 100-yr time slices — Findings

**Input**: `data/capital.csv` (39 century bins, BCE 4300 → BCE 500, step −100; 12 Z-indicator columns). The Z columns are pre-standardized to mean ≈ 0 but have residual inequality in standard deviation (ZSichel std ≈ 0.53, others ≈ 0.97–0.99); the analysis re-standardizes each column to exact (mean 0, std 1) before PCA — this is mathematically equivalent to a correlation-based PCA on the "pseudo-Z" inputs.

**Method**: ONE PCA on the 39×12 exact-standardized matrix (numpy SVD; no `sklearn` available). All 12 components retained; PC1 (30.33%) and PC2 (19.47%) explored; PC1+PC2 cumulative 49.79%. Sign-alignment convention applied per researcher's instruction:
- PC1 flipped so that `ZKeform` (Pottery Form) loading is positive (raw PC1 loading on `ZKeform` was −0.3529 → flipped).
- PC2 alignment: variable with largest |loading| on PC2 is `ZBeil` (+0.4706 pre-flip) which was already positive → no PC2 sign flip.

**Verbatim PCA-output artefacts**:
- `artifacts/data/principal_compliance.json` ← machine-readable summary.
- `artifacts/data/pca_loadings_12x12.csv` ← PC1..PC12 loadings + per-PC1/PC2 contribution shares.
- `artifacts/data/pca_scores_39bins.csv` ← per-bin (BCE, group) PC1..PC12 scores.
- `artifacts/data/symbolic_on_PC1_PC2.csv` ← focused row-table for `Zhausgr / ZDolch / ZAxtSchwert`.
- `artifacts/data/capital_standardized.csv` ← the exact-standardized 39×12 matrix fed into PCA.
- `artifacts/data/pca_run.log` ← full stdout of the executed script.
- `artifacts/analysis/pca_capital_100yr.py` ← the executed script (numpy-only SVD).

## Std-dev verification

All 12 inputs verified to have mean ≈ 0 (max |mean| ≈ 0.001; mean ≈ 0 across the 39 bins) but variable std before re-standardization: range [0.53, 0.99]. After re-standardization (subtract column mean, divide by column std): all 12 columns have std = 1.0 exactly. PCA was therefore run on the correlation-equivalent matrix.

